      "content": "Thought: Skip connections alone perform poorly (0.153), confirming that convolutional operations are necessary for good performance. The all 3x3 conv baseline (0.709) is much better. Let me try a mixed approach with 1x1 convolutions which are computationally cheaper than 3x3 but still learn features, combined with some 3x3 convs.\n\nAction: evaluate_config {\"1<-0\": \"nor_conv_1x1\", \"2<-0\": \"nor_conv_3x3\", \"2<-1\": \"nor_conv_1x1\", \"3<-0\": \"nor_conv_3x3\", \"3<-1\": \"nor_conv_1x1\", \"3<-2\": \"nor_conv_3x3\"}"
